# T257. This directory is Convoke's own REPOSITORY-audit tooling: it scans the source tree and
# writes frozen inventories that CI and migrations consume. `files[]` carried `scripts/` whole, so
# all 26 files reached every operator install — `backlog-integrity.js`, which prints
# `FAIL — backlog not found at …`; `coverage-denominator.js`, which shells out to `git ls-files`
# and dies on git's own `fatal: not a git repository` (that text is git's stderr, not a string in
# the file);
# `try-fresh-install.sh`; and, the reason this is more than untidiness,
# `pf1-judge-calibration.js` and `pf1-validation-battery.js`, which `require('@anthropic-ai/sdk')`
# — a devDependency ABSENT from `dependencies`, so it throws for an operator — and read
# `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.
#
# WHY HERE AND NOT A `!` NEGATION IN `files[]`. Story dist-2.3a settled this for
# scripts/migration/format-conversion and the reasoning transfers verbatim: a negation puts a glob
# metacharacter into `files[]`, which `scripts/audit/lib/installed-tree.js` parses to build the
# expected set of `_bmad/bme/*` modules, and four hand-written attempts to tell a harmless
# negation from a coverage-shrinking one were all broken by adversarial review.
# `tests/lib/format-conversion-exclusion.test.js` asserts `files[]` carries no metacharacter at
# all, and a `"!scripts/audit/**"` entry fails it — measured, which is how this file came to exist
# after the negation had already been written and packed.
#
# THE THREE UN-IGNORES ARE NOT OPTIONAL and not a style choice. npm force-includes a `bin` target
# over `files[]` but NOT over a `.npmignore` — measured both ways: with a bare `*` here, all three
# bins vanish from the tarball and `convoke-audit-bmm-deps`, `convoke-audit-skill-dirs` and
# `convoke-validate-marketplace` become dead entry points. These three are exactly the files a
# declared `bin` resolves to, and none of them requires anything else under this directory.
#
# `!audit-bmm-dependencies.js` CARRIES MORE THAN ITS OWN BIN, and describing the three as merely
# "the bin targets" understates it. That file is a MODULE-SCOPE require of `convoke-doctor.js`
# and `convoke-register-skill.js` — two bins that are NOT under this directory — so losing this
# one line stops them loading at all, not just `convoke-audit-bmm-deps`. Measured: remove the
# file and both throw out of the CJS loader before printing anything.
#
# What would catch that: `scripts/audit/try-fresh-install.sh` installs the real tarball and runs
# `assert-installed-tree.js requires` over every bin with a TRANSITIVE worklist, failing closed,
# and ci.yml runs it (`run: bash scripts/audit/try-fresh-install.sh`). That gate is stronger than
# a static check over a pack listing, which is why no new test was added here for this property.
#
# This list duplicates `package.json`'s `bin` map, which is the hazard this repo keeps paying for.
# It is bound rather than trusted: `tests/lib/skills-packaging.test.js` derives the expected set
# FROM `bin` and asserts tarball equality, so adding a fourth audit bin without a line here, or
# leaving a line here after retiring a bin, turns that test red.
#
# NOT DELETED, and must not be: every tool here is live repository tooling, several are wired into
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, and `scripts/audit/lib/installed-tree.js` backs the installed-tree
# gate. Removing them from the PACKAGE is not removing them from the repository.
*
!audit-bmm-dependencies.js
!audit-skill-dirs.js
!validate-marketplace.js
